fastlowess provides the upstream CMake target:

    find_package(fastlowess CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE fastlowess::fastlowess)

This port installs a checksum-pinned upstream CPU library for Windows x64/ARM64,
Linux x64/ARM64, or macOS x64/ARM64. Linux triplets containing `musl` select the
musl build; other Linux triplets select the glibc build. Shared linkage is
required. Use dynamic-linkage triplets such as `x64-linux-dynamic`,
`arm64-linux-dynamic`, `x64-osx-dynamic`, or `arm64-osx-dynamic`; default static
Linux/macOS triplets are unsupported. Windows uses the dynamic MSVC runtime and
generates its import library from the verified export list. Debug and Release
consumers both use the upstream Release library. Rust and Cargo are not required.